th dogs get a morning walk),\n   output ONE entry per pet with the SAME start_time and task_name so they can be merged.\n5. If the owner specified a time for a task, use that exact time.\n6. If no time was specified, choose a sensible time within the available window.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON \u2014 no extra text.\n\nRequired JSON format:\n{\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"task_name\": \"Morning Walk\",\n      \"start_time\": \"7:00am\",\n      \"duration\": 30,\n      \"priority\": 5,\n      \"pet_name\": \"Buddy\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"One or two sentences explaining your scheduling decisions.\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Only schedule tasks inside the available window\n- Never schedule during blocked times\n- Use 12-hour format for start_time (e.g. \"7:00am\", \"6:30pm\")\n- duration is an integer number of minutes\n- priority is an integer 1\u20135 (5 = highest)\n- Space tasks realistically throughout the day\n- Do NOT add tasks the owner did not request"}
